Single migration history for backend-owned product tables.

Issue #60: upgrade to 1b2c3d4e5f6a before deploying scoped invitation creation.
The migration removes global key uniqueness and adds atomic actor/Team/operation
records with normalized request hashes. Existing invitations and tokens survive;
legacy keys cannot replay because their creating actor was never recorded.

Prefer a forward fix when rolling back. Downgrade discards scoped replay records
and restores global uniqueness; it refuses while duplicate raw invitation keys
exist across scopes. Stop invitation writes and resolve those duplicates before
attempting a downgrade. Do not rewrite invitation tokens or delivery state.
